    "diagnosis": "<p>Pleomorphic liposarcoma</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>Note that most of the lesion shows spindle cells and such foci cannot be diagnosed as pleomorphic liposarcoma. Pleomorphic liposarcoma is diagnosed on H&amp;E staining by identifying pleomorphic lipoblasts, as in the upper left of the image, in which lipid droplets crisply indent the pleomorphic nucleus. Sometimes examination of multiple tissue blocks is required to identify the diagnostic areas, which can be missed on needle biopsies.</p>",
